<title>JAPAN: Nippon Credit down on profit-taking and rating cut.</title>
<headline>Nippon Credit down on profit-taking and rating cut.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nippon Credit Bank Ltd fell on Monday morning as profit-taking set in following a technical jump late last week, brokers said.</p>
<p>They added that a bond ratings cut by Moody's Investors Service on Friday was also dampening sentiment.</p>
<p>As of 0146 GMT, the shares were down 17 yen at 284 yen, the third largest percentage loser on the first section of the Tokyo bourse. It was also the most heavily traded issue, with trade totalling about 5.24 million shares.</p>
</text>
